<title>USA: New UK Govt not seen thwarting merger--AMR.</title>
<headline>New UK Govt not seen thwarting merger--AMR.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Robert Crandall, chairman and CEO of AMR Corp., parent company of American Airlines, said Wednesday he did not think the new Labour Party government in Britain would make the airline's proposed merger with British Airways less likely.</p>
<p>Asked by Cable News Network if he thought the recent victory by the Labour Party would make the proposed merger less likely, Crandall said &quot;No.&quot; He then added. &quot;Of course we don't know what the Labor government's attitude will be.&quot;</p>
</text>
